FlipBase for the Miyoo Flip
===========================

Called BaseOS until it moved to mainline Linux; renamed FlipBase as it is now an
independent project. Derived from BaseOS for Allwinner H700 handhelds by Prashant Vaibhav:

    https://github.com/pvaibhav/BaseOS

Forked at commit dbe5211 ("docs: update README.md", 2026-08-15). The full upstream
history is preserved in this repository's git history; upstream authorship is intact
on every commit that carries it.

Files that remain upstream's work, unmodified or nearly so:

    src/fbsplash.c              the framebuffer splash renderer
    src/gptgrow.c               first-boot expand-to-fill; rewritten to read the
                                GPT geometry from the header instead of hardcoding
                                the H700 layout
    src/gptslot.c               A/B slot arithmetic; rewritten around this card's
                                three slotted regions and header-derived geometry
    src/gpt.h                   the CRC and entry helpers both of them share
    tools/mkupdate.py           update payload builder; extended to three regions
    board/my355/rootfs-overlay/usr/sbin/flipbase-update
                                the update engine, adapted to this layout
    flash-card.sh               macOS card writer; reduced to one target, and its
                                disk guard rekeyed on removable and virtual media

Taken later, from upstream commit 7dec5cb (2026-09-18):

    board/my355/rootfs-overlay/usr/sbin/flipbase-config
                                the flipbase.conf parser; reduced to hostname and
                                ssh_password, with a fixed default hostname
    board/my355/assets/flipbase.conf
                                its template, since extended with FlipBase's
                                own settings
    tests/test-flipbase-config.sh its tests, adapted to the above

board/my355/assets/boot.ttf is licensed under the SIL Open Font License; see
board/my355/assets/OFL.txt.

Everything else — the Rockchip boot chain, the SPI NAND preloader work, the
Buildroot tree and packages, the my355 rootfs, overlay and documentation — is new
in this repository.

MAINLINE LINUX
--------------

The move to mainline Linux was made possible by Zetarancio's reverse-engineering
of the Miyoo Flip and their mainline port, zlyme:

    https://github.com/Zetarancio/Miyoo-Flip-Mainline-Linux-Reverse-Engineering

FlipBase's device tree and several of its drivers follow that work, and the
patches taken from it keep Zetarancio's authorship in their headers. Other pieces
come from ROCKNIX's Miyoo Flip support and upstream Rockchip patches.

VENDOR FIRMWARE
---------------

FlipBase boots the vendor's BL31 and OP-TEE, and loads the vendor's Bluetooth
firmware. Both come from the stock firmware:

    uboot.img           Miyoo's Rockchip U-Boot FIT, whose BL31, OP-TEE and
                        control device tree are used verbatim
    stock-harvest.tar   allowlisted paths from the stock squashfs, of which
                        the build takes rtl8733bu_fw and rtl8733bu_config

Neither is committed to this repository. They are published as a release
artifact, pinned by hash in package/stock-firmware/, which can be pointed at a
dump of your own unit instead.

Publishing that bundle redistributes Miyoo's firmware. Miyoo has not granted
permission to do so, and parts of it are third-party works under their own terms
(the Linux kernel is GPL-2.0 and its source has not been published for this build;
glibc is LGPL; the Mali userspace is ARM proprietary).

KERNEL SOURCES
--------------

board/my355/linux/ holds patches, drivers and a device tree for Linux, and is
GPL-2.0 like the kernel it builds into, as each driver's SPDX line says. The
patches in package/mali-kbase/ and package/rtl8733bu/ are GPL-2.0 like the
out-of-tree drivers they apply to. Where a piece comes from Zetarancio, ROCKNIX
or upstream, the origin is noted in the file or in docs/mainline-compat.md.

The patches in patches/ and package/ for other software are under that
software's license.

